Get-Process

Displays all currently running processes on the system.

Why This Command Matters Useful for: Monitoring system performance  Identifying high CPU or memory usage

Detailed Explanation A process is any running application or background service  
PowerShell displays processes as objects, not plain text  This allows advanced filtering, sorting, and automation

Common Parameters 
-Name → View a specific process  
-Id → View a process by ID

Example:
Get-Process | Sort-Object CPU -Descending

Displays running processes sorted by CPU usage  Helps identify performance bottlenecks



